e. So, is Dave young or old? From statement 3, Bob is young. Statement 7, Gary is young. So, Dave's age isn't specified. But from statement 11, young things are nice, which Dave is, but that doesn't necessarily mean he's young. So Dave could be either young or old.\n\nIf Dave is young, then from statement 15, since he's quiet, he would be red. But from statement 9, he's white. So that's a contradiction. Therefore, Dave cannot be young. Therefore, Dave must be old.\n\nSo Dave is old, big, round, nice, quiet, and white. Now, from statement 15, old, loud things are blue. But Dave is quiet, so he's not loud. Therefore, statement 15 doesn't apply to Dave. So Dave's color is white.\n\nWait, but from statement 15, it's about old, loud things being blue. Since Dave is old but quiet, he doesn't fall into that category. So his color is white.\n\nTherefore, Dave is white, not red. So the statement \"Dave is not red\" is true.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought he was black. I must have made a mistake in my initial reasoning. Let me clarify.\n\nFrom statement 10: If something is big and white, then it's round. So, if something is round, it's big and white? No, statement 10 is a one-way implication. It says if big and white, then round. It doesn't say that all round things are big and white. So, round things are nice (statement 8), but not necessarily big and white unless they are big and white.\n\nSo, Dave is round, so he's nice. From statement 13, he's quiet. From statement 14, he's big. From statement 9, since he's nice and big, he's white. So Dave is big, round, nice, quiet, and white.\n\nNow, from statement 15: Young, quiet things are red. Since Dave is quiet, if he were young, he'd be red. But Dave is not young because he's old (as established earlier). Therefore, Dave is white, not red.\n\nSo the statement \"Dave is not red\" is true.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A) True\n\nDave is round, which makes him nice. Being nice and big (from being round and quiet), he is white. Since he's old and quiet, he doesn't fall under the category of being red. Therefore, Dave is not red.\n\nThe correct option is: A",
