ot red. So that changes everything.\n\nSo Anne is green and young. So the statement \"Anne is young\" is true. So the answer is A) True.\n\nWait, but let me check if any rules affect this. Point 11 says all nice, green people are young. So if Anne is green and nice, she must be young. But we know she's young, so that's consistent.\n\nPoint 16 says if Anne is nice and not white, then she's green. Since she's green, that condition is satisfied. But we don't know if she's nice or not. However, point 9 says if someone is white, they are nice. But Anne isn't white because she's green. So she might not be nice, but she could be nice for other reasons.\n\nBut regardless, the fact that she's young is given directly in point 2. So the statement is true.\n\nSo the correct answer is A) True.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
