statement 12).\n2. If Bear is rough \u2192 Bear needs rabbit (statement 10).\n3. If Bear needs rabbit \u2192 Rabbit sees squirrel (statement 11).\n4. Rabbit needs squirrel (statement 6) \u2192 Rabbit sees squirrel.\n5. If someone needs rabbit and rabbit sees mouse \u2192 Mouse sees rabbit (statement 9).\n6. Mouse sees rabbit? No, statement 5 says the mouse doesn't see the rabbit.\n7. Therefore, if the bear is rough, then the mouse should see the rabbit, but it doesn't. Contradiction.\n\nTherefore, the assumption that the bear is rough leads to a contradiction, so the bear cannot be rough. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False",
