rom fact 15: Furry, blue things are red. But Bob is blue and red, but we don\'t know if he\'s furry.\n\nWait, but Bob is red, so from fact 18, he\'s round. So Bob is round.\n\nBut from fact 16, if he\'s round and big, he\'s blue. So Bob is blue.\n\nBut from fact 13, blue → white. So Bob is white.\n\nBut from fact 15, if he\'s furry and blue, he\'s red. But we don\'t know if Bob is furry.\n\nWait, but the initial facts don\'t mention Bob being furry. So Bob is big, cold, red, round, blue, and white.\n\nBut the question is whether Bob is not round. From the above, Bob is round. So the statement "Bob is not round" is false.\n\nWait, now I\'m getting conflicting conclusions. Earlier, I thought Bob is flat, but that was based on a wrong assumption.\n\nLet me correct that. Fact 18 says all red things are round. So Bob is red → Bob is round.\n\nFact 16 says if something is round and big, then it\'s blue. So Bob is round and big → Bob is blue.\n\nFact 13 says all blue things are white. So Bob is white.\n\nFact 15 says furry, blue things are red. But Bob is blue and red, but we don\'t know if he\'s furry.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Bob is big → cold → red → round. And since he\'s round and big, he\'s blue. So Bob is blue, red, round, big, and white.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Bob is not round" is false because Bob is round.\n\nSo the correct answer is B) False.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought Bob is flat because blue things are flat, but that\'s incorrect because fact 18 says red things are round, not blue things. Fact 13 says blue things are white, but it doesn\'t say anything about being flat or round. So my initial mistake was assuming blue things are flat, but that\'s not the case.\n\nSo, to clarify:\n\n- Bob is big → cold → red → round (from fact 18).\n- Bob is round and big → blue (from fact 16).\n- Bob is blue → white (from fact 13).\n\nSo Bob is round, so the statement "Bob is not round" is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Bob is big (Fact 7).**\n2. **Big → Cold (Fact 19).** Therefore, Bob is cold.\n3. **Cold → Red (Fact 14).** Therefore, Bob is red.\n4. **Red → Round (Fact 18).** Therefore, Bob is round.\n5. **Round and Big → Blue (Fact 16).** Therefore, Bob is blue.\n6. **Blue → White (Fact 13).** Therefore, Bob is white.\n\nSince Bob is round, the statement "Bob is not round" is false.\n\n**Answer:** B) False', ''] 24%|##4       | 147/600 [1:14:24<6:02:09, 47.97s/it]
