's check point 8: all smart people are furry.Since Erin is smart, she must be furry.So Erin is furry.\n\nNow, since Erin is smart and furry (from point 8 and 10), she should be round.But wait, point 6 says if someone is round, they are blue.We already know Erin is blue, so that\'s consistent.But does that mean Erin is round?\n\nWait, let me make sure. Point 10 says dumb, scaly people are flat. Erin is dumb and scaly, so she must be flat. Therefore, Erin is flat.\n\nBut the question is asking if Erin is round. So if Erin is flat, then the statement "Erin is round" is false. Therefore, the answer should be A) True.\n\nWait, but let me double-check. Is there any contradiction here? Let\'s see:\n\n- Erin is warm and dumb (given).\n- Dumb and warm → black (point 7).\n- Black → if Erin is black, then green (point 5).\n- Green → dumb (point 11), which is inconsistent.\n- Dumb → scaly (point 8).\n- Dumb and scaly → flat (point 10).\n- Flat → green (point 6), which is inconsistent because Erin is green.\n\nSo all the conditions point to Erin being flat. Therefore, the statement "Erin is round" is true.\n\n']]
