he statement we\'re evaluating is "Charlie is rough." If Charlie is smooth, then the statement is true. So the answer would be A) True.\n\nBut let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything. Let\'s go through the steps again.\n\nCharlie is green (point 5). From point 13, green implies not blue. So Charlie is not blue. From point 8, not blue implies not rough. Therefore, Charlie is not rough. So the statement "Charlie is rough" is true.\n\nI do see contradictions here. All the rules point towards Charlie not being rough. So the correct answer should be A) True.\n']]
