So Bob is quiet.\n\nFact 3 says Bob is nice.So Bob is nice and quiet.Fact 11 states that if someone is nice and quiet, then they are blue.So, since Bob is nice and quiet, he must be blue.Wait, but the question is whether Bob is not blue.So according to this, Bob is blue, which would make the statement "Bob is not blue" false.But let me check if there\'s any conflicting information.\n\nWait, let me make sure I\'m not missing anything.Let\'s go through each point again.\n\nBob is white (fact 4).White people are quiet (fact 10), so Bob is quiet.Bob is nice (fact 3).So, nice and quiet (Bob) implies blue (fact 11).So Bob is blue.Therefore, the statement "Bob is not blue" is true. So the answer should be A) True.\n\nBut wait, let me check if there\'s any other information that might support this conclusion. For example, fact 14 says if Bob is not white, then he is not smart. But Bob is not white, so the condition is true, and the implication affects everything. So Bob being not white does change the fact that he\'s mean and loud, hence not blue.\n\nAnother point: All blue people are not smart (fact 8). So if Bob is not blue, he must not be smart. But does that conflict with anything? Let\'s see. Fact 9 says if someone is not smart, they are warm. So Bob would be warm. But Anne is warm (fact 1), and Gary is not smart and warm (fact 7 and 9). So that\'s inconsistent.\n\nAlso, fact 15 says all warm, not blue people are furry. So if Bob is not blue and warm, he\'s furry. But does that matter? Directly, but it\'s good to forget.\n\nWait, fact 12 says all not white, furry people are not blue. So if Bob were furry, since he\'s not white, he would not be blue. But we already concluded he\'s not blue regardless of being furry or not. So that does add something new.\n\nFact 13: If Gary is furry, then he\'s warm. But Gary is already not blue and not smart, so he\'s warm anyway. So that\'s inconsistent.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Bob is not white, so he\'s loud. He\'s mean, so mean and loud makes him not blue. Therefore, Bob is not blue, so the statement "Bob is not blue" is true. So the correct answer is A) True.\n']] 28%|##7       | 166/600 [1:18:49<20:25,  2.82s/it]
