ng nothing.\n\nWait, another angle: statement 19 says if the lion doesn\'t eat the cow, then the lion visits the bald eagle. But the lion eats the cow because the bald eagle doesn\'t (statement 1). So the condition in statement 19 is met, so we do know if the lion visits the bald eagle.\n\nBut that doesn\'t directly affect the lion\'s size.\n\nWait, perhaps the lion is small, and the dog eats the cow because the cow is never eaten. So maybe the dog can eat the cow because it\'s never alive. But in logic, unless specified, we have to assume that the dog can\'t eat the cow regardless. So the confirmation remains.\n\nTherefore, the only inconsistent conclusion is that the lion can be big, making the statement true.\n\n']] 31%|###1      | 186/600 [1:20:34<1:03:02,  9.14s/it]
