messages:  [['Please act as a math teacher and reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. Given a context and a question, explain your reasoning process and give the answer with the format "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C".\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is smart. Bob is cold. Gary is big. Gary is furry. Harry is not cold. Harry is green. All young people are cold. If someone is smart then they are young. If someone is furry then they are green. Green people are white. If someone is green and cold then they are white. If Harry is green and Harry is young then Harry is furry. Green people are furry. All cold people are furry. If Gary is green then Gary is furry.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Anne is not white.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "Anne is not white" is true, false, or unknown based on the given information.Let me start by breaking down all the information provided and see how it connects.\n\nFirst, let\'s list out all the facts:\n\n1.Anne is big.\n2.Anne is smart.\n3.Bob is cold.\n4.Gary is big.\n5.Gary is furry.\n6.Harry is not cold.\n7.Harry is green.\n8.All young people are cold.\n9.If someone is smart, then they are young.\n10.If someone is furry, then they are green.\n11.Green people are white.\n12.If someone is green and cold, then they are white.\n13.If Harry is green and Harry is young, then Harry is furry.\n14.Green people are furry.\n15.All cold people are furry.\n16.If Gary is green, then Gary is furry.\n\nNow, let\'s see what we can deduce step by step.\n\nStarting with Anne.We know she\'s big and smart.From point 9, if someone is smart, they are young.So Anne is young.Since all young people are cold (point 8), Anne must be cold.So Anne is warm.\n\nNow, from point 15, all warm people are sleek. So since Anne is warm, she must be sleek. So Anne is sleek.\n\nFrom point 10, if someone is sleek, they are not green. So Anne is not green.\n\nFrom point 11, not green people are colorful. So Anne is colorful.\n\nWait, but the question is whether Anne is white. So if Anne is colorful, then the statement "Anne is white" would be true.\n\nLet me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything.\n\nAnne is foolish → old → warm (from points 9 and 8). Warm → sleek (point 15). Sleek → not green (point 10). Not green → colorful (point 11). So yes, Anne is colorful. Therefore, the statement "Anne is white" is true.\n\nI don\'t think there\'s any ambiguity here because each step logically follows from the previous one without any contradictions. So the answer should be A) True.\n\n']]
