f Charlie were round, then according to fact 12, Charlie would not be young. But we know Charlie is young, so that creates a contradiction. Therefore, Charlie cannot be round.\n\nWait, let me make sure I\'m following that correctly. Fact 12 is an if-then statement: If someone is round AND nice, then they are not young. So, the contrapositive would be: If someone is young, then they are not both round and nice. But Charlie is young, nice, and smart. So, if Charlie were round, then according to fact 12, Charlie would not be young. But Charlie is young, so that can\'t be. Therefore, Charlie cannot be round.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Charlie is young, nice, smart, and furry. Since being round would contradict the fact that Charlie is young and nice, Charlie must not be round.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Charlie is round" is false.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False\n\nCharlie is not round because being round would contradict the fact that he is young and nice, as per the given conditions.', '']
