ot).\n- The squirrel doesn\'t need the rabbit (from statement 14, because the squirrel visits the mouse and the mouse doesn\'t need the squirrel).\n\nSo, the squirrel doesn\'t need the rabbit, but the bear\'s needs are mentioned that it\'s cruel. There\'s a statement that says the bear doesn\'t need the rabbit or anything else.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, we have many statements that directly and indirectly link the bear needing the rabbit. So, the statement "The bear doesn\'t need the rabbit" is known because there\'s information provided about the bear\'s needs beyond being cruel and being avoided by the mouse.\n\n']]
