final_output:  ['Wait, but the question is whether the lion likes the bald eagle. So, if the lion dislikes the bald eagle, then the statement is false.\n\nBut let me make sure I didn\'t make a mistake.\n\nFrom statement 17: If X likes the dog, then X likes the bald eagle. But in our case, the lion dislikes the dog, so the contrapositive would be: If X does not like the bald eagle, then X does not like the dog. Wait, no, the contrapositive of "If A then B" is "If not B then not A." So, the contrapositive of statement 17 is: If X does not like the bald eagle, then X does not like the dog.\n\nBut we know that the lion dislikes the dog, so according to the contrapositive, the lion must dislike the bald eagle.\n\nTherefore, the lion does not like the bald eagle, so the statement is false.\n\nWait, but let me check again. The lion dislikes the dog, so according to statement 17, the lion must dislike the bald eagle. So, the statement "The lion likes the bald eagle" is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False', '']
