en they are furry.\n\nFiona is white and smart (from being big, statement 15).So Fiona is furry.\n\nHarry is white and smart, so Harry is furry.\n\nNow, statement 10: All furry people are white, which is consistent.\n\nNow, can we determine if Gary is white?\n\nWe don\'t have any information that directly links Gary to being white or not.\n\nStatement 11 requires quiet and cold to be white.Gary is quiet, but we don\'t know if he\'s cold.\n\nIs there any other way to determine Gary\'s color?\n\nLooking at statement 13: If Harry is big, then Harry is cold.Harry is big, so he\'s cold.\n\nBut that doesn\'t help with Gary.\n\nIs there any other rule that could make Gary white?\n\nStatement 8 requires white and smart to be furry, but we don\'t know if Gary is white.\n\nAlternatively, if Gary is furry, he must be white (statement 10).But we don\'t know if he\'s furry.\n\nSo, without knowing if Gary is cold, we can\'t apply statement 11 to him.\n\nTherefore, we don\'t have enough information to determine if Gary is white, and thus we can\'t determine if he\'s furry.\n\nWait, but let\'s think again.\n\nStatement 15: If someone is big, then they are smart.\n\nStatement 14: If someone is big and smart, then they are quiet.\n\nSo, all big people are smart and quiet.\n\nNow, statement 11: If someone is quiet and cold, then they are white.\n\nSo, for someone to be white, they need to be quiet and cold.\n\nBut we don\'t know if Gary is cold.\n\nIs there any other way to determine if Gary is cold?\n\nLooking at the given statements, the only people who are cold are Fiona and Harry (from statements 2 and 13).There\'s no information about Gary being cold.\n\nTherefore, we can\'t assume Gary is cold.\n\nThus, we can\'t apply statement 11 to Gary, so we don\'t know if he\'s white.\n\nSince we don\'t know if Gary is white, and we don\'t have any other information that would make him furry, we can\'t determine if he\'s furry.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Gary is furry" is unknown.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought Fiona and Harry are white and furry, but what about others?\n\nBob is big, so he\'s smart and quiet, but we don\'t know if he\'s cold or white.\n\nSo, Bob could be white if he\'s cold, but we don\'t know.\n\nSimilarly, Gary could be white if he\'s cold, but we don\'t know.\n\nTherefore, the answer is unknown.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C) Unknown', ''] 60%|#####9    | 359/600 [2:23:32<1:00:40, 15.10s/it]
