t statement 18 was about visiting the bald eagle if you chase the dog, but maybe I misread it. Let me check again.\n\nStatement 18: \"If someone chases the dog, they visit the bald eagle.\" So, yes, if the tiger chases the dog, then the tiger visits the bald eagle. So, the statement is true.\n\nBut wait, another angle: does the tiger actually visit the bald eagle? Or is it just that the tiger chases the dog, which according to statement 18, implies visiting the bald eagle. So, the conclusion is that the tiger does visit the bald eagle.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) True.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
