tement "The squirrel is blue" is false.\n\nWait, but the question is about the squirrel being blue. Since the squirrel is green, the statement is false.\n\nWait, but I\'m getting confused again. Let me make a table.\n\nEntities:\n\n- Bald eagle: chases squirrel, eats dog\n- Bear: eats bald eagle, eats dog\n- Dog: chases bald eagle, chases bear, chases squirrel, eats squirrel, is big, is blue, is green\n- Squirrel: is green\n\nSo, the squirrel is green. Therefore, the statement "The squirrel is blue" is false.\n\nWait, but the dog is blue, so maybe the squirrel is also blue? No, because the squirrel is explicitly green. So, the squirrel is green, not blue.\n\nTherefore, the statement is false.\n</think>\n\nThe squirrel is explicitly stated to be green, so the statement that it is blue is false.\n\nThe correct option is: B) False', '']
