ut we don't know if Harry is green.\n\nWait, but if Harry is rough, he must be green (fact 16). If he's green and rough, he must be quiet (fact 13). But Harry is not quiet (since he's not cold, and quiet things are cold). Therefore, Harry cannot be both green and rough. So if Harry were rough, he would have to be green, which would make him quiet, but he's not quiet. Therefore, Harry cannot be rough.\n\nTherefore, Harry is not rough. So the statement \"Harry is not rough\" is true.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought Harry could be smooth because he's yellow. But now I'm getting that Harry cannot be rough because that would make him quiet, which he's not. So Harry must be smooth.\n\nSo the statement is true.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A) True",
