y must be rough, so the statement is true.\n\nBut wait, let me make sure I didn't miss any other rules that might affect this.\n\nRule 8: If someone is rough and young, then they are cold.\n\nGary is young and, according to our deduction, rough. So he must be cold.\n\nBut the facts say Gary is green and young, but not cold. However, from rule 6: Young people are cold. So Gary must be cold.\n\nSo, Gary is cold, green, young, nice, quiet, and rough.\n\nTherefore, the statement \"Gary is rough\" is true.\n\nSo the correct answer is A) True.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
