ld eagle visits the tiger.\n\nTherefore, the tiger visits the lion, making the statement false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False\n\nThe reasoning is as follows:\n\n1. The bald eagle is young (fact 3), so it needs the tiger (fact 24).\n2. Since the bald eagle needs the tiger, it visits the tiger (fact 20).\n3. If someone visits the tiger, then the tiger visits the lion (fact 17).\n4. Therefore, the tiger visits the lion, making the statement \"The tiger does not visit the lion\" false.\n\nThe correct option is: B) False",
