's conflicting with my earlier conclusion. Let me clarify.\n\n- Squirrel is red (statement 7) \u2192 young (statement 8).\n- Young \u2192 sees the mouse (statement 11). So, squirrel sees the mouse.\n- Squirrel eats the rabbit (statement 6) and sees the mouse (from above) \u2192 mouse is red (statement 12).\n- Mouse is red \u2192 young (statement 8).\n- Young \u2192 sees the mouse (statement 11). So, mouse sees itself.\n\nTherefore, the mouse does see itself, making the statement \"The mouse does not see the mouse\" false. So, the correct answer is B) False.\n\nI think that's the correct reasoning.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False",
