t 15, since he\'s quiet, he\'s round, which we already know.\n\nSo, all the facts point to Charlie being green. Therefore, the statement "Charlie is not green" is false.\n\nWait, but I\'m getting conflicting conclusions. Earlier, I thought Charlie is green, but then I considered that if he\'s big, he\'s not green, but since he\'s round, he\'s green, so he must be small. Therefore, he\'s green. So the statement is false.\n\nBut wait, let me make sure I\'m not missing any other implications. For example, fact 16: If someone is kind and not blue, then they are round. Charlie is not kind, as we don\'t have any information about his kindness. So that doesn\'t apply to him.\n\nSo, in conclusion, Charlie is green, so the statement "Charlie is not green" is false.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False\n\nCharlie is round, and according to the given information, if someone is round, they are green. Therefore, Charlie is green, making the statement "Charlie is not green" false.', '']
