final_output:  ['</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Bob is cold** (Fact 3).\n2. **All cold people are furry** (Fact 15). Therefore, Bob is furry.\n3. **If someone is furry, they are green** (Fact 10). Therefore, Bob is green.\n4. However, **Harry is not cold** (Fact 6) and **Harry is green** (Fact 7). From Fact 14, green people are furry, so Harry is furry.\n5. **If someone is green and cold, they are white** (Fact 12). Harry is not cold, so this doesn\'t apply.\n6. **Green people are white** (Fact 11). Harry is green, so he is white.\n7. **If someone is green and young, they are furry** (Fact 13). Harry is green and not cold, so he must be young (since all young people are cold, but Harry is not cold, so he\'s not young). This creates a contradiction because Harry is green and not young, but Fact 13 implies if he were young, he\'d be furry, which he is.\n8. **Gary is big and furry** (Facts 4 and 5). From Fact 10, Gary is green. From Fact 14, Gary is furry, so he\'s green. From Fact 16, if Gary is green, he\'s furry, which he is.\n9. **Anne is smart and young** (Facts 2 and 9). From Fact 8, she\'s cold. From Fact 15, she\'s furry. From Fact 10, she\'s green. From Fact 11, she\'s white.\n10. **Bob is cold, so he\'s furry (Fact 15). If he\'s furry, he\'s green (Fact 10). Therefore, Bob is green.**\n\n**Conclusion:** The statement "Bob is green" is **True**.\n\n**Final Answer:** The correct option is: A) True', '']
