og. The rabbit is nice (statement 10). If the rabbit eats the mouse, then the mouse chases the dog. But we don't know if the rabbit eats the mouse.\n\nStatement 11: If someone chases the dog, then the dog likes the cat. The cat chases the rabbit (statement 1), but does the rabbit chase the dog? Not stated. So, we don't know.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the only direct information about the rabbit is that it chases the mouse and is nice. There's no statement that directly says the rabbit likes the mouse or dislikes it. The conditionals don't give us enough information to conclude because they depend on other factors that aren't confirmed.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, it's unknown whether the rabbit likes the mouse.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C) Unknown", '']
