art. If Erin is foolish, then the statement "Erin is smart" would be true.\n\nLet me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything. Erin is blue, so round. That makes her mean. Mean people are foolish, so Erin is foolish. Therefore, the statement that Erin is smart is true.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions in the given information. All the premises lead to Erin being foolish. So, the answer should be that the statement is true.\n\n']]
