alse.\n\nWait, but let me make sure. Erin is red, so not round. Therefore, by point 11, she is nice. Nice people are smart, so Erin is smart. Therefore, the statement "Erin is not smart" is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer should be B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) False\n\nStep-by-step explanation:\n\n1. Erin is red (given).\n2. All red people are not round (given), so Erin is not round.\n3. Since Erin is red and not round, according to the conditional statement, she is nice.\n4. Nice people are smart (given), so Erin is smart.\n5. Therefore, the statement "Erin is not smart" is false.\n\nThe correct option is: B) False', '']
